WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.468 --> 00:00:01.868
They pledge to defend the law,

00:00:02.968 --> 00:00:04.370
represent the will of the people,

00:00:05.750 --> 00:00:10.833
but time and again elected officials have sold their soul and betrayed us all from bottom of the hat.

00:00:13.234 --> 00:00:15.995
Some countries are little more than mafia nations.

00:00:52.311 --> 00:00:52.451
Once

00:00:52.531 --> 00:00:54.871
an organized crime group gets a grip on society,

00:00:55.173 --> 00:00:56.454
it is very difficult to break.

00:00:57.695 --> 00:00:57.975
Why?

00:00:58.815 --> 00:00:59.156
Simple.

00:01:00.280 --> 00:01:04.763
Crime bosses know that the secret to maintaining their power is to corrupt their greatest adversary,

00:01:05.644 --> 00:01:06.325
the government.

00:01:16.573 --> 00:01:16.912
Today,

00:01:17.013 --> 00:01:19.855
organized crime has been traced to all regions of the globe.

00:01:25.663 --> 00:01:26.987
One of the most distinguishing,

00:01:27.107 --> 00:01:28.030
albeit regrettable,

00:01:28.090 --> 00:01:32.222
characteristics of the 20th century has been the proliferation of organized crime.

00:01:36.120 --> 00:01:44.183
The transformation of the Mafia into an organization with a managerial hierarchy occurred when the fabric of America was undergoing a major alteration.

00:01:45.164 --> 00:01:49.344
East Harlem was a really tough immigrant neighborhood.

00:01:49.385 --> 00:01:49.645
I mean,

00:01:49.724 --> 00:01:50.585
it was poor,

00:01:50.826 --> 00:01:51.626
it was violent,

00:01:51.706 --> 00:01:52.546
it was squalid,

00:01:52.667 --> 00:01:53.527
it was crowded.

00:01:56.584 --> 00:01:57.405
Really the modern

00:01:58.165 --> 00:02:06.091
American Mafia as we know it was born up on those streets in the boyhood rumbles of guys like Luciano,

00:02:06.331 --> 00:02:07.071
Lucchese,

00:02:07.131 --> 00:02:08.212
and Frank Costello,

00:02:08.412 --> 00:02:09.913
and Vita Genovese.

00:02:10.293 --> 00:02:11.074
They all knew each other.

00:02:11.254 --> 00:02:12.655
the same what was called a bogata.

00:02:13.415 --> 00:02:15.016
Bogata means like a gang,

00:02:15.177 --> 00:02:16.879
a gang of delinquent boys.

00:02:18.140 --> 00:02:21.983
And every block in an Italian neighborhood had a social club.

00:02:23.224 --> 00:02:26.546
And when they walked past the social club they saw something very different.

00:02:28.328 --> 00:02:29.249
Guys in suits,

00:02:29.609 --> 00:02:30.390
beautiful suits,

00:02:31.330 --> 00:02:31.931
fedoras.

00:02:33.879 --> 00:02:36.262
Italian handmade shoes,

00:02:37.804 --> 00:02:38.905
big beautiful cars,

00:02:40.246 --> 00:02:40.506
women.

00:02:41.507 --> 00:02:42.268
Kids like Luce,

00:02:42.608 --> 00:02:43.728
they wanted to hang around,

00:02:43.729 --> 00:02:44.990
because what did they see?

00:02:45.490 --> 00:02:46.852
They saw the American dream,

00:02:47.572 --> 00:02:47.832
money,

00:02:48.693 --> 00:02:49.174
power.

00:02:49.493 --> 00:02:50.754
Nobody bothered these guys.

00:02:52.437 --> 00:02:54.759
Once Luciano's boyhood gang became organized,

00:02:55.459 --> 00:02:59.383
they soon graduated from rumbles and petty crime to more sophisticated rackets.

00:03:03.943 --> 00:03:06.004
Soon the gangsters were rolling in cash.

00:03:07.444 --> 00:03:09.104
As this new mafia's power grew,

00:03:09.306 --> 00:03:10.925
they expanded into other rackets,

00:03:11.485 --> 00:03:11.966
gambling,

00:03:12.026 --> 00:03:12.787
prostitution,

00:03:12.807 --> 00:03:13.567
and narcotics.

00:03:14.567 --> 00:03:16.266
Law enforcement attempted to stop them,

00:03:16.707 --> 00:03:19.828
but the gangsters had already put their newfound wealth to good use,

00:03:21.489 --> 00:03:22.569
buying off policemen,

00:03:22.709 --> 00:03:23.088
judges,

00:03:23.109 --> 00:03:23.689
and mayors.

00:03:26.670 --> 00:03:29.290
Others were just too frightened to stop the growth of the mob.

00:03:35.587 --> 00:03:37.187
Cooperation of local government,

00:03:37.649 --> 00:03:41.030
Luchano's crime syndicate established a stranglehold on the city.

00:03:47.411 --> 00:03:49.012
Luchano's story is not unique.

00:03:51.051 --> 00:03:54.173
The cocaine cartels of Colombia began in much the same way.

00:03:56.114 --> 00:03:57.794
Colombia's biggest drug kingpin,

00:03:57.894 --> 00:03:58.813
Pablo Escobar,

00:03:59.155 --> 00:04:02.776
forged a crime empire by corrupting his government on a massive scale.

00:04:06.963 --> 00:04:10.426
Escobar had a simple method of influencing judges and politicians.

00:04:11.147 --> 00:04:13.650
He would send an attorney to offer the official a choice.

00:04:14.230 --> 00:04:15.352
Plomo or plata?

00:04:16.012 --> 00:04:17.153
Lead or silver?

00:04:18.134 --> 00:04:19.456
If he did not take the bribe,

00:04:19.976 --> 00:04:22.678
he and his family could expect to get a bullet instead.

00:04:25.797 --> 00:04:27.738
Because of his power and because of his,

00:04:28.799 --> 00:04:29.399
I would say,

00:04:30.960 --> 00:04:31.900
just brute force,

00:04:31.920 --> 00:04:33.661
he was able to influence a lot of people.

00:04:34.001 --> 00:04:34.862
The people heard,

00:04:35.082 --> 00:04:37.183
especially judges and prosecutors in Colombia,

00:04:37.203 --> 00:04:38.724
would hear the name Pablo Escobar,

00:04:39.084 --> 00:04:42.546
they would feel like there was a death threat and they would not get in his way.

00:04:43.886 --> 00:04:47.348
At one point there was no one in the entire country Escobar could not buy,

00:04:47.508 --> 00:04:47.948
silence,

00:04:48.048 --> 00:04:48.469
or kill.

00:04:50.445 --> 00:04:50.825
In fact,

00:04:50.845 --> 00:04:52.065
when he was finally convicted,

00:04:52.626 --> 00:04:57.907
officials on Escobar's payroll allowed him to build his own prison that was more like a hacienda.

00:05:04.069 --> 00:05:05.690
It's the same old story in Japan.

00:05:06.790 --> 00:05:09.691
Authorities are struggling to free themselves from the grip of the Yakuza.

00:05:10.971 --> 00:05:14.632
The Japanese syndicate has so entwined itself into business and government,

00:05:14.832 --> 00:05:16.853
the three are virtually indistinguishable.

00:05:20.985 --> 00:05:24.388
They recruit the unemployed to the political corridors of government.

00:05:25.489 --> 00:05:26.710
They can be deeply religious,

00:05:27.370 --> 00:05:28.251
kind and thoughtful,

00:05:29.172 --> 00:05:32.114
but can be as ruthless as Japan's World War II image.

00:05:33.155 --> 00:05:35.877
They currently operate beyond the laws and in secret.

00:05:39.320 --> 00:05:40.901
With the decay of the communist system,

00:05:41.382 --> 00:05:44.244
there was little left to separate the Russian mafia from the government.

00:05:46.513 --> 00:05:53.790
Corruption is so widespread in Russia that officials simply buy their positions and use their power to conduct criminal operations.

00:05:58.993 --> 00:06:12.623
The Russians are particularly different than other mafia groups because they have a level of professionalism that really comes from their long record of being able to deal with a very difficult totalitarian system.

00:06:12.663 --> 00:06:13.644
They know how to get around it,

00:06:13.724 --> 00:06:14.925
they know how to get around the police,

00:06:15.346 --> 00:06:18.048
they know how to suborn and corrupt officialdom.

00:06:18.928 --> 00:06:24.432
And most of them are quite shrewd and intelligent businessmen.

00:06:26.849 --> 00:06:29.951
Slums are often the home of neighborhood gangs of one type or another.

00:06:31.111 --> 00:06:34.793
But hoodlum gangs have become organized crime groups with billion-dollar assets.

00:06:36.013 --> 00:06:37.334
This happened in Jamaica in the

00:06:37.714 --> 00:06:41.736
80s, when a street thug named Jim Brown teamed up with the nation's president.

00:06:47.097 --> 00:06:49.759
Brown came out of one of the toughest neighborhoods in Kingston.

00:06:50.619 --> 00:06:52.000
He grew up poor and hungry.

00:06:52.961 --> 00:06:56.923
But his appetite for wealth led to a life of crime that landed him in prison.

00:06:58.524 --> 00:07:04.588
His story is a classic example of what can happen when government officials become partners in crime.

00:07:05.848 --> 00:07:06.189
Good day,

00:07:06.269 --> 00:07:06.529
Mr.

00:07:06.549 --> 00:07:06.789
Brown.

00:07:08.941 --> 00:07:11.142
The British Privy Council have reviewed your appeal.

00:07:11.803 --> 00:07:12.643
I'm afraid you lost.

00:07:13.744 --> 00:07:17.025
The federal marshals are on their way to extradite you to the United States.

00:07:18.446 --> 00:07:18.566
Oh,

00:07:18.766 --> 00:07:20.447
they can't wish they never did that.

00:07:22.769 --> 00:07:24.169
They all love the money I give.

00:07:25.330 --> 00:07:26.170
The politicians.

00:07:26.771 --> 00:07:27.611
They're the criminals.

00:07:28.932 --> 00:07:29.972
You want to eat in this country,

00:07:29.992 --> 00:07:31.313
you've got to play by their rules.

00:07:32.294 --> 00:07:33.815
That's how I came to be locked up here.

00:07:34.515 --> 00:07:36.856
Playing by their rules all my life.

00:07:38.725 --> 00:07:40.567
You see,

00:07:40.568 --> 00:07:41.748
I was one of the Sufferer Youth.

00:07:42.268 --> 00:07:43.069
The Sufferer Youth?

00:07:43.990 --> 00:07:44.190
Oh,

00:07:44.551 --> 00:07:46.713
that's the quaint phrase they give to the poor,

00:07:46.853 --> 00:07:48.034
misbegotten youth of...

00:07:50.877 --> 00:07:51.317
Forgive me,

00:07:51.537 --> 00:07:51.778
Mr.

00:07:51.818 --> 00:07:52.038
Brown.

00:07:52.939 --> 00:07:54.440
You don't know nothing,

00:07:54.500 --> 00:07:54.720
man.

00:07:55.882 --> 00:07:56.402
I suppose,

00:07:56.403 --> 00:07:56.903
in a sense,

00:07:56.904 --> 00:07:57.964
you are quite correct.

00:07:59.986 --> 00:08:00.686
Please continue.

00:08:00.726 --> 00:08:02.668
You were saying you were part of the Suffering Youth.

00:08:05.529 --> 00:08:06.990
We had nothing.

00:08:07.510 --> 00:08:08.611
Not even enough to eat.

00:08:09.592 --> 00:08:12.294
The police and the government were getting fat off their own people.

00:08:13.395 --> 00:08:15.676
When that hurricane money came down to help the people,

00:08:15.756 --> 00:08:16.817
where do you think it goes to?

00:08:17.698 --> 00:08:18.178
The people?

00:08:19.960 --> 00:08:20.440
No man,

00:08:20.500 --> 00:08:21.821
it goes in their pockets.

00:08:22.882 --> 00:08:24.823
We have to have crime to live.

00:08:25.764 --> 00:08:27.425
To take our peace back from them.

00:08:28.926 --> 00:08:31.868
We gotta have the policies to protect ourselves from the cops who are gonna kill us.

00:08:43.294 --> 00:08:47.036
The typical childhood of a suffering youth in Jamaica.

00:08:48.657 --> 00:09:01.224
is a very frightening one in the sense that many of that generation were simply not able to have access to high schools.

00:09:01.684 --> 00:09:01.904
I mean,

00:09:01.984 --> 00:09:05.506
their schooling would end at the age of 14 or 15.

00:09:06.346 --> 00:09:11.010
It would mean then that just hosing would be a serious problem.

00:09:12.090 --> 00:09:15.933
Getting food on a daily basis would be a serious problem.

00:09:16.394 --> 00:09:21.157
Many of these people depended on remittances coming from abroad.

00:09:21.597 --> 00:09:21.838
I mean,

00:09:22.158 --> 00:09:26.701
that really sometimes determined whether they survived or did not survive.

00:09:27.202 --> 00:09:27.662
And of course,

00:09:27.722 --> 00:09:30.964
growing up in those communities with the level of violence,

00:09:31.465 --> 00:09:32.706
you really had to be tough.

00:09:33.106 --> 00:09:34.187
in order to survive,

00:09:34.207 --> 00:09:38.530
and it was very difficult to survive if you didn't develop a certain inner toughness.

00:09:40.451 --> 00:09:42.672
The government gave you a good job building houses,

00:09:42.733 --> 00:09:43.073
didn't it,

00:09:43.093 --> 00:09:43.353
Mr.

00:09:43.373 --> 00:09:43.573
Brown?

00:09:44.814 --> 00:09:46.835
You mean that welding shop on Milk Lane?

00:09:47.736 --> 00:09:50.237
The only time I made money was during the elections.

00:09:51.178 --> 00:09:51.979
The elections?

00:09:53.320 --> 00:09:53.500
Look,

00:09:53.700 --> 00:09:56.262
it's not just elections here.

00:09:57.546 --> 00:10:01.509
The way things work in Jamaica is that neighborhoods get favors.

00:10:01.950 --> 00:10:04.192
Like housing developments from politicians.

00:10:05.393 --> 00:10:06.153
To get favors,

00:10:06.154 --> 00:10:08.455
they got to vote for that guy when he's running for president.

00:10:09.716 --> 00:10:10.097
I see.

00:10:11.017 --> 00:10:13.419
But what does that have to do with your welding business?

00:10:13.800 --> 00:10:14.640
Where you come from?

00:10:15.481 --> 00:10:16.282
You don't think?

00:10:17.423 --> 00:10:18.904
Now if you know where the neighborhoods are,

00:10:18.905 --> 00:10:20.045
they're going to vote for your enemy.

00:10:20.345 --> 00:10:21.066
What you going to do?

00:10:22.927 --> 00:10:24.509
You burn them out.

00:10:28.354 --> 00:10:34.778
The posse's came up at the same time as Jamaica's politics were polarized in the

00:10:35.799 --> 00:10:41.823
1970s. By the time Michael Manley became Prime Minister in 1972 and Edward Seaga,

00:10:41.824 --> 00:10:43.304
the leader of the Jamaica Labour Party,

00:10:43.324 --> 00:10:46.668
party had emerged as his nemesis on the right.

00:10:47.129 --> 00:10:52.775
The two men were really engaged in a vicious power struggle for dominance in Jamaica.

00:10:53.556 --> 00:10:57.221
Seaga's tactics were always known to be extraordinarily dirty.

00:10:58.262 --> 00:11:00.404
He was perfectly willing to use violence.

00:11:01.244 --> 00:11:09.251
And most Jamaicans will tell you that it was the JLP that really upped the ante of violence in Jamaica's politics in the

00:11:10.312 --> 00:11:15.516
1970s. Michael Manley retaliated by developing his own garrisons.

00:11:15.676 --> 00:11:25.624
And the level of this warfare is almost impossible for an American to understand because it involves strategies and tactics such as burning people out of their homes.

00:11:26.325 --> 00:11:28.026
there's an area that's known to

00:11:28.086 --> 00:11:33.350
be packed with supporters of one party and you're in the other party and you want to unseat them.

00:11:33.870 --> 00:11:48.320
You simply torch that that neighborhood by night and shoot at the firemen as they're trying to put out the blaze and when the blaze is over you bulldoze the rubble and build a housing scheme as it's called in Jamaica,

00:11:48.360 --> 00:11:49.481
a housing project,

00:11:49.541 --> 00:11:51.943
and you pack it full of your own supporters.

00:11:52.303 --> 00:11:55.946
It was a no-holds-barred undeclared civil war.

00:11:56.426 --> 00:11:58.747
It was extraordinary in its viciousness,

00:11:59.427 --> 00:12:03.028
and Jamaicans very soon began to call it tribal war.

00:12:03.408 --> 00:12:12.150
Violence had become so much a way of life in Jamaica's politics that neither political party seemed willing to try to extirpate it.

00:12:13.751 --> 00:12:16.592
While Jim Brown profited from this political turf war,

00:12:17.532 --> 00:12:21.493
he soon realized that the real power was not in the contracting business,

00:12:22.293 --> 00:12:24.954
but within Jamaica's corrupt political structure.

00:12:26.426 --> 00:12:30.669
So you became involved in organized crime through the president of Jamaica?

00:12:32.611 --> 00:12:32.791
Well,

00:12:32.831 --> 00:12:34.472
he's the biggest crook on the island

00:12:35.713 --> 00:12:38.055
When I seen how President Seaga had all this power,

00:12:38.735 --> 00:12:40.616
I decided I need to get closer to the top.

00:12:41.717 --> 00:12:45.200
So I pick up a gun and I start to work for Seaga as an enforcer.

00:12:46.961 --> 00:12:47.802
I was good with a gun.

00:12:49.503 --> 00:12:50.283
People on the street,

00:12:50.343 --> 00:12:51.124
they know my name.

00:12:52.265 --> 00:12:52.965
They're afraid of me.

00:12:54.978 --> 00:12:58.379
Soon I become Seaga's bodyguard and right-hand man.

00:12:59.919 --> 00:13:01.840
Now when the election comes and Seaga wins,

00:13:02.400 --> 00:13:03.060
that's good for me.

00:13:03.961 --> 00:13:05.221
I could get some of that power too.

00:13:06.521 --> 00:13:07.482
And for the other side,

00:13:08.402 --> 00:13:09.222
we got rid of them.

00:13:09.962 --> 00:13:16.284
After President Seaga won the 1980 election,

00:13:16.944 --> 00:13:20.145
the gunmen that helped him to gain power became a force in their own right.

00:13:21.145 --> 00:13:22.806
Brown is Seaga's right-hand man.

00:13:23.198 --> 00:13:24.880
Coming dawn of Jamaica's underworld,

00:13:25.540 --> 00:13:27.262
his rivals were running scared.

00:13:29.964 --> 00:13:35.669
And these gangsters began to go out of Jamaica after the 1980 election,

00:13:35.709 --> 00:13:38.291
when they were essentially on the run for their lives.

00:13:38.692 --> 00:13:39.432
They saw that

00:13:39.873 --> 00:13:40.873
Seaga had won.

00:13:41.954 --> 00:13:44.316
Anybody who had fired shots for the PNP,

00:13:44.737 --> 00:13:45.738
the rival party,

00:13:46.238 --> 00:13:48.480
knew that they really had to get out of Jamaica.

00:13:55.976 --> 00:13:57.136
With the competition gone,

00:13:57.196 --> 00:13:58.477
Jim Brown's power grew.

00:13:59.257 --> 00:14:02.778
He had established himself as a godfather of Jamaica's drug mafia.

00:14:04.039 --> 00:14:06.939
But the war on drugs was beginning in the United States,

00:14:07.220 --> 00:14:10.581
and law enforcement was cracking down on Jamaica's greatest export,

00:14:11.061 --> 00:14:11.621
marijuana.

00:14:11.641 --> 00:14:18.003
They can't get the shipments through,

00:14:18.023 --> 00:14:21.044
so now we got a big load of guns just sitting on the docks at Kingston.

00:14:21.324 --> 00:14:26.006
Does it surprise you that the Americans don't want you shipping drugs to their country?

00:14:26.186 --> 00:14:31.549
You don't understand what I'm talking about.

00:14:31.550 --> 00:14:33.370
If the ganja don't go out,

00:14:34.010 --> 00:14:36.772
then a lot of Jamaicans are going to be hungry.

00:14:39.328 --> 00:14:43.330
But I know a lot of people now in places in Jamaica and Miami,

00:14:43.590 --> 00:14:44.670
in places in the States.

00:14:45.611 --> 00:14:47.531
So that's when I start shipping the ganja out,

00:14:47.952 --> 00:14:49.292
and then the money starts to come in.

00:14:49.612 --> 00:14:50.573
So you got rich.

00:14:51.353 --> 00:14:52.634
Everybody got some of the money.

00:14:53.374 --> 00:14:55.034
The posses aren't just gangs.

00:14:56.295 --> 00:14:59.096
We're like the guys we used to see in those movies back in Kingston.

00:15:00.237 --> 00:15:02.277
We made our own justice.

00:15:11.677 --> 00:15:14.378
There is a gun culture in Jamaican society.

00:15:15.218 --> 00:15:23.961
There is a fascination for guns and of course one of the things about guns is that when you put guns in the hands of poor people or sufferer youths,

00:15:24.661 --> 00:15:31.323
it is a form of empowerment and it gives them a sense that they have control over life and death.

00:15:35.396 --> 00:15:48.420
What was happening on the streets downtown in Kingston was a growing fascination with the Hollywood silver screen and primarily the outlaws and cowboys and bandits that came out of Hollywood in the

00:15:48.780 --> 00:15:50.040
50s and 60s and early 70s.

00:15:53.041 --> 00:16:04.644
The gangsters who were by then up and coming in the ranks of both parties began to style themselves after these cowboy heroes And that became the real kind of...

00:16:05.312 --> 00:16:08.877
emotional substance that the gangs carried to

00:16:09.317 --> 00:16:10.218
Kingston's poor.

00:16:11.019 --> 00:16:13.482
That was just something that Jamaicans adored,

00:16:13.923 --> 00:16:16.846
because their own lives were nasty and short,

00:16:17.447 --> 00:16:19.570
and when they looked at Hollywood movies,

00:16:19.610 --> 00:16:23.334
they felt as if those movies were really telling the story of their lives.

00:16:27.152 --> 00:16:32.094
Brown quickly formed his Jamaican connections into an organized crime group called the Shower Posse.

00:16:33.154 --> 00:16:35.855
Named for their ability to shower their enemies with bullets,

00:16:36.335 --> 00:16:38.396
the group brought Havoc to the United States.

00:16:38.816 --> 00:16:41.697
Brown decided to expand his drug dealing operations.

00:16:45.738 --> 00:16:45.858
So,

00:16:46.718 --> 00:16:48.279
once you were in control in Jamaica,

00:16:49.519 --> 00:16:52.140
what made you decide to return to the United States?

00:16:54.994 --> 00:16:56.015
Or was it the money again?

00:16:56.016 --> 00:16:57.396
The shower was making money.

00:16:57.857 --> 00:16:59.538
We were selling in Washington,

00:16:59.919 --> 00:17:00.419
New York,

00:17:00.559 --> 00:17:00.980
Miami.

00:17:01.400 --> 00:17:03.542
We were making money hand over fist.

00:17:04.624 --> 00:17:07.687
But there were a lot of other gunmen from Jamaica trying to sell drugs.

00:17:08.548 --> 00:17:09.549
We had to get rid of them.

00:17:10.430 --> 00:17:14.574
There was this reggae club where those guys went.

00:17:15.355 --> 00:17:16.055
We followed them.

00:17:28.484 --> 00:17:29.045
We just,

00:17:29.685 --> 00:17:30.446
forgive the pun,

00:17:31.386 --> 00:17:32.647
showered them with bullets,

00:17:33.528 --> 00:17:35.049
even the innocent bystanders.

00:17:35.549 --> 00:17:37.270
Anybody goes against me,

00:17:37.670 --> 00:17:38.511
they're going to die.

00:17:39.071 --> 00:17:40.032
People have asked,

00:17:40.652 --> 00:17:42.194
if these men are so violent,

00:17:43.094 --> 00:17:46.857
and if they kill so many of their own in the line of duty,

00:17:46.957 --> 00:17:47.457
so to speak,

00:17:47.777 --> 00:17:51.380
why is it that Jamaicans see them as heroic?

00:17:51.904 --> 00:17:53.045
as Robin Hood,

00:17:53.305 --> 00:17:54.465
Defenders of the Poor.

00:17:54.585 --> 00:17:56.106
And the reason for this,

00:17:57.066 --> 00:18:00.428
and it's really the most important and exhalant fact,

00:18:01.128 --> 00:18:03.549
the drug trade became the only game in town.

00:18:04.890 --> 00:18:05.450
These men,

00:18:05.530 --> 00:18:08.652
men like Jim Brown and his shower posse,

00:18:09.192 --> 00:18:10.452
became the people,

00:18:11.053 --> 00:18:11.953
the only people,

00:18:12.033 --> 00:18:14.314
who were putting shoes on the feet of children,

00:18:14.714 --> 00:18:16.975
who were putting roofs over people's heads,

00:18:17.476 --> 00:18:18.236
so that when...

00:18:18.700 --> 00:18:21.864
Somebody needs money to pay a child's school entrance fee.

00:18:22.224 --> 00:18:24.186
They're going to turn to their local posse.

00:18:24.667 --> 00:18:28.771
That's who they're going to go to for help because they can't go to the government anymore.

00:18:31.234 --> 00:18:33.376
These fools in some crack house in Miami.

00:18:34.917 --> 00:18:36.319
When we rolled up in front of the place,

00:18:36.819 --> 00:18:38.061
I just felt this anger.

00:18:38.882 --> 00:18:40.163
I burst in and shot the guy.

00:18:46.752 --> 00:18:49.096
Who was this woman there?

00:18:53.042 --> 00:18:53.964
She was pregnant.

00:18:56.888 --> 00:18:58.090
That was very brave of you.

00:19:02.112 --> 00:19:03.513
I did what I had to do.

00:19:06.316 --> 00:19:06.917
A man try to...

00:19:09.680 --> 00:19:11.061
A man try to mash my corn,

00:19:11.301 --> 00:19:13.043
he better know I'm gonna mash his corn back,

00:19:13.243 --> 00:19:14.665
and his whole field too.

00:19:16.307 --> 00:19:18.609
And did President Sayaga know about all of this?

00:19:19.250 --> 00:19:20.391
The corn mashing,

00:19:20.591 --> 00:19:21.252
as you put it?

00:19:21.532 --> 00:19:23.094
Who you think I learned it from?

00:19:26.428 --> 00:19:29.570
The shower posse was gaining wealth and power through the drug trade,

00:19:30.070 --> 00:19:34.933
but the very tools they used to enforce their grip on their turf would prove to be their undoing.

00:19:36.014 --> 00:19:37.575
We needed the guns to keep control,

00:19:39.916 --> 00:19:42.118
but when they were used too much in the States,

00:19:42.498 --> 00:19:44.919
then we shipped them down to Jamaica so we could use them again.

00:19:45.660 --> 00:19:47.841
We packed them away good to hide them from customs.

00:19:48.562 --> 00:19:51.703
I don't know how those guns...

00:19:53.700 --> 00:19:54.661
At that point,

00:19:55.321 --> 00:19:58.744
he was also sending firearms back to Jamaica.

00:19:59.265 --> 00:20:01.126
In 1984,

00:20:01.127 --> 00:20:03.308
the shower tried to send,

00:20:03.388 --> 00:20:04.929
did send down to Jamaica,

00:20:05.510 --> 00:20:09.854
an enormous shipment of firearms that wound up on the Kingston Warbs,

00:20:10.294 --> 00:20:11.715
and someone was tipped off,

00:20:11.875 --> 00:20:14.317
and so the person who was to claim it never did.

00:20:14.898 --> 00:20:19.141
When they opened the barrel and found these high-powered weapons,

00:20:19.562 --> 00:20:22.324
this was the first time that Interpol...

00:20:22.524 --> 00:20:27.909
the International Police Organization was called in to try to track the source of these guns.

00:20:28.469 --> 00:20:38.499
And it was discovered that some of these same guns that had been sent in this barrel back to Jamaica had been used in homicides in the United States.

00:20:39.039 --> 00:20:48.528
And it was really that shipment of guns to Jamaica in 1984 that first alerted international law enforcement to the presence of the posses.

00:20:51.308 --> 00:20:53.810
Once law enforcement identified the shower posse,

00:20:54.170 --> 00:20:57.592
they began to target them for prosecution as an organized crime group.

00:20:58.493 --> 00:21:02.996
The RICO statute is a statute aimed at corrupt organizations,

00:21:03.737 --> 00:21:05.698
racketeering-influenced corrupt organizations.

00:21:06.519 --> 00:21:11.922
And it's designed to target an organization,

00:21:12.283 --> 00:21:13.464
legitimate or illegitimate,

00:21:13.544 --> 00:21:15.485
that is corrupt in some way.

00:21:16.606 --> 00:21:19.568
A coordinated effort led by...

00:21:19.904 --> 00:21:21.226
The New York office of the FBI,

00:21:21.307 --> 00:21:23.230
in conjunction with the New York City Police Department,

00:21:23.531 --> 00:21:27.398
targeted numerous locations known to be used by the posse,

00:21:28.079 --> 00:21:30.543
used as either residences or...

00:21:31.756 --> 00:21:34.018
warehouses for cash and guns and drugs.

00:21:35.920 --> 00:21:38.482
Numerous Posse members were arrested that night,

00:21:38.662 --> 00:21:39.683
taken into federal custody.

00:21:41.785 --> 00:21:44.027
Automatic weapons were seized.

00:21:44.607 --> 00:21:46.729
Large amounts of marijuana,

00:21:47.089 --> 00:21:48.791
cocaine and heroin were also seized.

00:21:51.160 --> 00:21:54.102
Law enforcement was successful in breaking up the shower posse.

00:21:55.003 --> 00:21:56.584
Now they set their sights on its leader,

00:21:57.024 --> 00:21:57.565
Jim Brown.

00:21:58.425 --> 00:22:03.289
So American law enforcement was beginning to feel that it could go up against these gangs and win.

00:22:06.331 --> 00:22:14.637
There had been so many homicides by that time attributed to Jim Brown and the shower that the alcohol,

00:22:14.677 --> 00:22:15.117
tobacco,

00:22:15.197 --> 00:22:16.078
and firearms,

00:22:16.098 --> 00:22:16.698
the DEA,

00:22:16.938 --> 00:22:17.899
the FBI,

00:22:18.519 --> 00:22:19.620
the New York Police Department,

00:22:20.180 --> 00:22:26.404
and the Metro Dade Police Department felt that if they could get Jim Brown back to the United States,

00:22:26.964 --> 00:22:29.125
they could prosecute him and win.

00:22:31.206 --> 00:22:34.428
So once they found these guns and linked you to another murder,

00:22:36.629 --> 00:22:38.310
they didn't charge you,

00:22:38.430 --> 00:22:40.592
deported you to Jamaica to stand trial?

00:22:41.232 --> 00:22:44.033
I was President Seaga's right-hand man.

00:22:45.074 --> 00:22:46.215
I'm an untouchable.

00:22:47.175 --> 00:22:48.496
So you were just let off.

00:22:48.596 --> 00:22:49.417
for these murders.

00:22:50.398 --> 00:22:51.779
I keep Jamaica running.

00:22:52.099 --> 00:22:53.320
Of course they're going to let me go.

00:22:54.461 --> 00:22:58.024
Now the United States try to extradite me for those things I've done with shower posse.

00:22:59.125 --> 00:23:00.866
They put pressure on President Seaga.

00:23:01.587 --> 00:23:02.968
If he didn't extradite you,

00:23:03.108 --> 00:23:04.209
Jamaica would have suffered.

00:23:05.770 --> 00:23:08.012
I'm afraid the courts won't be so easy on you.

00:23:08.853 --> 00:23:11.555
The Americans take a very dim view of this sort of thing.

00:23:11.556 --> 00:23:13.196
I'll put Seaga where he is today.

00:23:14.357 --> 00:23:17.220
He wouldn't be president of Jamaica without me.

00:23:18.064 --> 00:23:19.705
I did most of those crimes for him.

00:23:20.886 --> 00:23:23.948
He wants to lock me away when he is just as guilty as me.

00:23:24.929 --> 00:23:26.610
I get a sense you feel betrayed.

00:23:27.030 --> 00:23:27.150
Oh,

00:23:27.250 --> 00:23:28.251
you've got that right,

00:23:28.331 --> 00:23:28.471
ma'am.

00:23:28.472 --> 00:23:29.672
If it's any consolation,

00:23:30.993 --> 00:23:31.673
you're not alone.

00:23:32.874 --> 00:23:35.576
President Seaga betrayed his oath of office,

00:23:36.457 --> 00:23:36.997
his country,

00:23:37.577 --> 00:23:38.178
his people,

00:23:39.619 --> 00:23:40.259
and of course,

00:23:41.260 --> 00:23:44.502
the suffering youth.

00:23:45.983 --> 00:23:46.964
Unfortunately...

00:23:49.532 --> 00:23:50.553
He had assistance,

00:23:51.013 --> 00:23:51.394
didn't he,

00:23:51.434 --> 00:23:51.694
Mr.

00:23:51.714 --> 00:23:51.994
Brown?

00:23:59.181 --> 00:24:01.023
You better think twice about sending me,

00:24:01.024 --> 00:24:03.245
because they will have a lot of questions about you.

00:24:04.526 --> 00:24:05.988
And I got a lot of answers.

00:24:09.351 --> 00:24:12.113
Before the United States Marshals arrived to pick up Brown,

00:24:12.554 --> 00:24:14.396
he was mysteriously killed in jail.

00:24:15.057 --> 00:24:16.658
burned alive in his cell.

00:24:18.140 --> 00:24:22.363
Jim Brown was going to be extradited to stand trial in the United States.

00:24:22.904 --> 00:24:28.769
Edward Seaga knew that if he were allowed to go back to the United States and talk,

00:24:29.409 --> 00:24:42.901
he would tell the federal authorities everything he knew about his connections to Seaga and the Jamaica Labor Party and the ways in which the party had aided and abetted the Shower Posse's exploits in the United States.

00:24:43.601 --> 00:24:52.668
Jim Brown was burned to death in a fire in his cell at Kingston's General Penitentiary in February of 1992 as U.S.

00:24:52.748 --> 00:24:57.012
federal marshals were waiting to take him back aboard a plane to Miami.

00:25:01.275 --> 00:25:09.802
When an enterprising young reporter at the funeral asked him to see Aga if Jim Brown had enjoyed the backing of a politician,

00:25:10.543 --> 00:25:13.065
Aga all but lost his temper with this man.

00:25:13.593 --> 00:25:19.997
And said that Jim Brown had been a defender of his community and a hero to the poor.

00:25:20.937 --> 00:25:22.678
And that sooner or later,

00:25:22.738 --> 00:25:25.880
Jamaicans would realize that such men were really heroic.

00:25:32.843 --> 00:25:36.045
I think what you can say about Jim Brown was that if you were a supporter,

00:25:36.085 --> 00:25:36.826
you adored him.

00:25:37.386 --> 00:25:38.727
And if you were an adversary,

00:25:38.767 --> 00:25:39.927
you were terrified of him.

00:25:42.369 --> 00:25:42.869
In China.

00:25:43.481 --> 00:25:45.743
Organized crime is as old as the country itself.

00:25:46.764 --> 00:25:48.706
As with various other old world nations,

00:25:48.826 --> 00:25:51.369
Chinese organized crime was always part of the culture.

00:25:52.390 --> 00:25:53.871
The exodus of the Chinese in the

00:25:54.632 --> 00:25:57.595
1800s exported Asian organized crime to the rest of the world.

00:25:58.776 --> 00:26:00.718
Soon Chinese syndicates were everywhere.

00:26:01.379 --> 00:26:03.321
They called themselves the Triad.

00:26:10.197 --> 00:26:15.899
Triads began when a Chinese emperor ordered the extermination of monks who were supreme martial arts masters.

00:26:21.581 --> 00:26:24.121
After their temple was burned and their members massacred,

00:26:24.442 --> 00:26:26.362
the surviving monks went underground.

00:26:29.243 --> 00:26:29.663
In fact,

00:26:29.664 --> 00:26:33.544
the term triad is derived from the triangle the monks used to represent heaven,

00:26:33.905 --> 00:26:34.145
earth,

00:26:34.345 --> 00:26:34.765
and man.

00:26:38.609 --> 00:26:39.990
With the fall of the last emperor,

00:26:40.570 --> 00:26:48.973
this secret organization prospered and established close connections to political figures who recruited the triad members as bodyguards and secret police.

00:26:52.115 --> 00:26:54.035
While triads performed a useful function,

00:26:54.496 --> 00:26:57.377
the arrival of the Communist Party in China spelled their doom.

00:26:59.318 --> 00:27:04.420
Party leader Mao Zedong's Cultural Revolution aimed to cleanse China of its old regime,

00:27:05.380 --> 00:27:06.661
including the triads.

00:27:16.285 --> 00:27:18.908
When Chiang Kai-shek fled with his army to Taiwan,

00:27:19.389 --> 00:27:21.832
the triads had found a perfect sanctuary.

00:27:23.605 --> 00:27:25.627
After 1949,

00:27:25.628 --> 00:27:27.408
the Triads only had one place to go,

00:27:27.688 --> 00:27:28.709
or two places really,

00:27:28.729 --> 00:27:31.892
to Hong Kong and then to Taiwan.

00:27:32.172 --> 00:27:35.775
And so they reestablished their ties with Taiwan.

00:27:36.115 --> 00:27:39.438
Chiang Kai-shek was able to utilize them as secret police.

00:27:39.858 --> 00:27:44.182
He was able to use them as hitmen when he began his rampage against the communists.

00:27:44.722 --> 00:27:47.464
Like every other political organization anywhere,

00:27:47.484 --> 00:27:48.645
you need some muscle.

00:27:49.266 --> 00:27:52.228
And he turned to them because of the most logical people to turn to.

00:27:54.553 --> 00:27:54.933
Generally,

00:27:55.493 --> 00:27:56.354
they played in very,

00:27:56.394 --> 00:27:57.614
very well with politics.

00:27:57.674 --> 00:27:57.854
Now,

00:27:58.335 --> 00:28:00.696
there is a connection between politics and the triad,

00:28:00.956 --> 00:28:02.537
but the triad has its place,

00:28:02.597 --> 00:28:08.459
and it has been used repeatedly by the politicians in China over the past

00:28:09.019 --> 00:28:09.640
50 years.

00:28:09.660 --> 00:28:10.040
In fact,

00:28:10.041 --> 00:28:10.720
they still are.

00:28:12.641 --> 00:28:16.743
It was in Taiwan that the triads began to take on a more sinister form.

00:28:20.004 --> 00:28:21.345
The first thing you have to understand...

00:28:22.005 --> 00:28:24.206
is that the triads aren't really gangs.

00:28:24.266 --> 00:28:26.726
They operate under a strict code of conduct and loyalty.

00:28:26.947 --> 00:28:27.867
They're all blood brothers.

00:28:28.807 --> 00:28:34.749
There's actually a ceremony where they mix each other's blood and tea and drink it.

00:28:35.009 --> 00:28:45.232
ROBERT STACK- An investigative reporter who wishes to remain anonymous for his own safety became familiar with Taiwan's underworld while working on a story about the country's largest triad,

00:28:45.632 --> 00:28:46.513
United Bamboo.

00:28:46.793 --> 00:28:49.654
That's when I decided to go after the head of United Bamboo.

00:28:50.813 --> 00:28:51.334
They called him

00:28:51.994 --> 00:28:52.514
White Wolf.

00:28:53.075 --> 00:28:54.916
Half of me wanted to see this guy busted.

00:28:56.317 --> 00:28:57.017
But I'm not a cop.

00:28:57.638 --> 00:28:58.578
I wanted his story.

00:29:00.500 --> 00:29:01.700
His real name was Shang Eng Lo.

00:29:02.161 --> 00:29:03.301
And in his mid-fifties,

00:29:03.302 --> 00:29:06.063
he was the honorary godfather of the 24 Tongs,

00:29:06.123 --> 00:29:06.243
or,

00:29:06.684 --> 00:29:07.104
gangs.

00:29:07.424 --> 00:29:10.546
With the billions he made in the various triad rackets,

00:29:10.967 --> 00:29:12.768
he could afford to keep himself in style.

00:29:14.941 --> 00:29:18.442
The reporter began with his triad contacts in Taiwan's underworld.

00:29:19.342 --> 00:29:23.283
Through a careful series of meetings with the lieutenants of the United Bamboo Triad,

00:29:23.583 --> 00:29:24.604
he gained their trust.

00:29:25.744 --> 00:29:30.945
The triads are organized under the head man or dragon head.

00:29:31.986 --> 00:29:35.867
You have different members responsible for such things as swearing in new soldiers,

00:29:35.887 --> 00:29:37.367
leading men into gang warfare,

00:29:37.427 --> 00:29:39.988
acting as liaisons between different triad groups.

00:29:41.208 --> 00:29:43.609
Under them are the soldiers and new recruits.

00:29:44.557 --> 00:29:44.697
Man,

00:29:44.737 --> 00:29:45.718
they're not just a gang.

00:29:46.539 --> 00:29:47.620
Everyone has his place.

00:29:48.340 --> 00:29:49.481
And if you step out of line,

00:29:50.502 --> 00:29:51.303
you pay the price.

00:29:53.044 --> 00:29:55.466
The reporter was finally cleared to meet the White Wolf.

00:29:56.087 --> 00:29:57.208
But with one condition.

00:29:57.768 --> 00:29:58.829
He was to come alone.

00:29:59.529 --> 00:30:01.611
And the White Wolf's face would not be shown.

00:30:02.132 --> 00:30:03.753
But he wasn't some flashy thug.

00:30:03.754 --> 00:30:05.775
He had five undergraduate degrees to his name.

00:30:05.815 --> 00:30:06.855
He was also bilingual,

00:30:07.196 --> 00:30:08.517
in English and Chinese.

00:30:09.877 --> 00:30:14.359
Tracking the leader of the Triads through the maze of the Chinese underworld seemed nearly impossible.

00:30:15.259 --> 00:30:15.700
Eventually,

00:30:15.701 --> 00:30:17.460
the reporter's persistence paid off.

00:30:21.762 --> 00:30:25.084
Or perhaps it was simply that the White Wolf had nothing to fear.

00:30:26.784 --> 00:30:27.004
Yes,

00:30:27.165 --> 00:30:27.465
Mr.

00:30:27.525 --> 00:30:27.905
Shang.

00:30:28.865 --> 00:30:29.105
Lately,

00:30:29.106 --> 00:30:33.827
we've all heard about the government crackdown on an organized crime group such as United Bamboo.

00:30:36.569 --> 00:30:37.349
Organized crime?

00:30:38.989 --> 00:30:39.589
You're mistaken.

00:30:40.530 --> 00:30:42.672
I am president of an investment company,

00:30:42.952 --> 00:30:43.872
the Strategy Group,

00:30:44.413 --> 00:30:47.775
similar to thousands of triad brothers who own legitimate concerns.

00:30:47.975 --> 00:30:50.057
They're simply arresting anyone who's a triad.

00:30:50.357 --> 00:30:51.337
With all due respect,

00:30:51.397 --> 00:30:51.698
Mr.

00:30:51.758 --> 00:30:52.078
Shang,

00:30:52.598 --> 00:30:54.219
what about the construction bids the

00:30:54.820 --> 00:30:58.242
Strategy Group rids through intimidation and government corruption?

00:30:58.842 --> 00:31:01.905
Politicians who have interest in construction make bids too.

00:31:03.345 --> 00:31:06.668
The triads had a contractor bid on a freeway construction job.

00:31:06.688 --> 00:31:08.329
He was up against a legitimate businessman.

00:31:08.845 --> 00:31:10.926
Of course the legitimate man's bid was lower.

00:31:11.166 --> 00:31:14.527
Triads have to inflate the budget of their project in order to skim money.

00:31:14.647 --> 00:31:15.968
They intimidate the bidders,

00:31:16.068 --> 00:31:17.509
threaten to kill their families.

00:31:17.669 --> 00:31:18.689
The bidders back off.

00:31:19.209 --> 00:31:23.311
Then the government official is more than happy to hand over the contract to his triad friends.

00:31:23.531 --> 00:31:25.592
And he looks clean.

00:31:27.613 --> 00:31:33.075
But the problem with the freeway construction job was that they skimmed so much money.

00:31:33.555 --> 00:31:34.835
There's no money left for building.

00:31:35.416 --> 00:31:36.736
Halfway through the project,

00:31:37.096 --> 00:31:38.377
a big section of the freeway...

00:31:39.981 --> 00:31:41.182
Just collapsed.

00:31:42.602 --> 00:31:43.943
That got the public's attention.

00:31:45.083 --> 00:31:46.024
I remember thinking,

00:31:46.624 --> 00:31:48.085
is this what I want for Taiwan?

00:31:48.665 --> 00:31:52.887
A core of corruption so rotten that the whole country collapses?

00:31:55.448 --> 00:31:57.949
Politicians who have interest in construction rig bids too.

00:31:58.629 --> 00:32:02.471
They accept a high bid on a job and skim the profits in their own pockets.

00:32:02.871 --> 00:32:04.472
Why single out the triad businessman?

00:32:05.572 --> 00:32:07.453
Would you rather we run opium dens?

00:32:08.033 --> 00:32:08.813
And number rackets?

00:32:08.953 --> 00:32:09.553
Basically,

00:32:10.234 --> 00:32:12.694
they'll do anything they can make money at.

00:32:13.415 --> 00:32:14.375
Prostitution,

00:32:14.795 --> 00:32:15.795
drug trafficking,

00:32:16.215 --> 00:32:17.036
gun smuggling,

00:32:17.196 --> 00:32:17.756
you name it,

00:32:17.776 --> 00:32:18.356
they're involved.

00:32:18.596 --> 00:32:26.038
But the most disturbing part of all this is that they have intertwined themselves with legitimate businesses and the government.

00:32:26.979 --> 00:32:27.999
They own big companies.

00:32:28.659 --> 00:32:32.320
They support the politicians with money and votes that are bought by the triads.

00:32:33.141 --> 00:32:34.261
And they're all in bed together.

00:32:36.217 --> 00:32:37.857
You rail against the politicians,

00:32:38.258 --> 00:32:40.418
but what are they left to do when the system's so corrupt?

00:32:40.478 --> 00:32:41.278
My point exactly.

00:32:41.398 --> 00:32:41.959
What am I to do?

00:32:42.619 --> 00:32:46.900
You can't separate triads from the government any more than you can peel yin from yang.

00:32:47.420 --> 00:32:49.181
How do you think President Lee got elected?

00:32:49.461 --> 00:32:51.001
Now he's the one leading the crackdown.

00:32:51.661 --> 00:32:53.142
The people were in an uproar.

00:32:53.882 --> 00:32:57.083
President Lee had no choice but to turn the heat up on the triads.

00:32:57.863 --> 00:32:58.843
There were many arrests,

00:32:59.543 --> 00:33:02.064
but the head of United Bamboo avoided capture.

00:33:11.105 --> 00:33:13.567
Whether it's the American mob or the Chinese triads,

00:33:14.007 --> 00:33:20.852
a gang's ascent to the ranks of large criminal enterprises comes when they learn that their biggest enemy can also be their greatest ally,

00:33:22.053 --> 00:33:22.993
their own government.

00:33:24.094 --> 00:33:25.375
This has happened in Mexico,

00:33:25.775 --> 00:33:27.737
with tragic results for law enforcement.

00:33:29.478 --> 00:33:32.620
Mexico shares a 2,000 mile border with the United States,

00:33:32.740 --> 00:33:35.602
and the drug traffickers no authorities can't patrol at all.

00:33:37.343 --> 00:33:39.845
Producing and shipping drugs has become big business.

00:33:41.029 --> 00:33:41.832
For the DEA,

00:33:42.233 --> 00:33:47.972
their only hope of stopping it is to go in undercover and bust drug trafficking operations at the source.

00:33:50.279 --> 00:33:57.623
A tragic case of DEA agent Enrique Camarena is a telling indictment of the Union of Government and Mafia drug lords.

00:34:01.765 --> 00:34:05.306
I guess you could say I was a casualty of the war on drugs.

00:34:07.888 --> 00:34:13.830
I was a DEA agent working undercover in Guadalajara,

00:34:13.911 --> 00:34:14.351
Mexico.

00:34:15.647 --> 00:34:16.988
Pretty gung-ho about it too.

00:34:18.370 --> 00:34:19.651
But I guess looking back on it,

00:34:19.652 --> 00:34:21.273
the only good thing was the food.

00:34:23.935 --> 00:34:25.677
Tracking these guys down wasn't hard.

00:34:26.938 --> 00:34:30.762
Mexico was full of hard-working families trying to make an honest living.

00:34:32.223 --> 00:34:35.366
These guys stuck out like sore thongs.

00:34:37.829 --> 00:34:38.229
Ernest

00:34:38.569 --> 00:34:39.130
Carrello

00:34:40.363 --> 00:34:42.364
He was the one who built up the drug cartel.

00:34:43.164 --> 00:34:46.626
He acted as a mentor to an up and coming drug lord named

00:34:46.966 --> 00:34:48.947
Rafael Caro Quintero.

00:34:51.068 --> 00:34:55.450
We knew Carillo and Quintero were both trafficking tons of drugs into the States.

00:34:56.810 --> 00:34:57.811
But looking back on it,

00:34:58.571 --> 00:35:01.052
we really didn't have a clue how big this thing was.

00:35:02.733 --> 00:35:04.213
Once I knew who the key players were,

00:35:05.314 --> 00:35:07.695
the next step was to locate their base of operations.

00:35:09.811 --> 00:35:11.192
Flying over the countryside,

00:35:11.232 --> 00:35:14.693
Camarena searched for drug plantations and processing facilities.

00:35:15.553 --> 00:35:18.254
He spotted a vast crop at a farm called El Buffalo,

00:35:18.674 --> 00:35:20.754
a marijuana plantation in Chihuahua,

00:35:21.034 --> 00:35:23.515
owned and operated by Rafael Caro Quintero.

00:35:29.297 --> 00:35:31.177
The DEA briefed the Mexican army.

00:35:31.638 --> 00:35:35.139
Together they organized a successful raid on Quintero's operation.

00:35:37.763 --> 00:35:38.603
But after the raid,

00:35:39.764 --> 00:35:40.925
something strange happened.

00:35:42.446 --> 00:35:45.027
All the expensive equipment at Old Buffalo vanished,

00:35:45.707 --> 00:35:47.108
even though it was under armed guard.

00:35:48.509 --> 00:35:49.509
And there was another thing.

00:35:50.610 --> 00:35:52.151
This was a gigantic operation.

00:35:53.091 --> 00:35:55.753
How did the Mexican police not know about this place before?

00:35:57.754 --> 00:36:01.056
I was beginning to wonder who was protecting Quintero.

00:36:01.776 --> 00:36:02.637
And just how I,

00:36:03.197 --> 00:36:04.057
his connections went.

00:36:04.138 --> 00:36:04.578
Business,

00:36:04.598 --> 00:36:04.918
you know?

00:36:05.478 --> 00:36:06.439
That's what we're doing here.

00:36:07.139 --> 00:36:07.919
Plain business.

00:36:07.920 --> 00:36:10.521
Caro Quintero was just a cowboy.

00:36:11.201 --> 00:36:13.322
He was rough and crude and brutal.

00:36:14.403 --> 00:36:17.485
The director of the Mexican Federal Police Force was Juan Zoria.

00:36:18.465 --> 00:36:23.008
Camarena began to suspect that the government official was protecting Mexican drug smugglers.

00:36:23.868 --> 00:36:24.809
Despite the danger,

00:36:25.309 --> 00:36:30.031
Camarena continued with his investigation of the drug lord and his political connections.

00:36:31.152 --> 00:36:34.634
He's being taken care of as we speak.

00:36:34.674 --> 00:36:36.335
I began wondering about Zorilla.

00:36:39.207 --> 00:36:41.568
I met him one time at one of those photo ops.

00:36:42.489 --> 00:36:43.970
Staged by the Mexican government.

00:36:46.631 --> 00:36:51.114
Zorilla and the DEA were teaming up to fight the war on drugs.

00:36:52.855 --> 00:36:53.555
What a joke.

00:36:59.078 --> 00:37:00.239
There's a saying in Mexico,

00:37:01.659 --> 00:37:02.260
the mordida,

00:37:02.920 --> 00:37:04.221
which means the bite.

00:37:06.002 --> 00:37:08.163
Nothing occurs in Mexico unless...

00:37:08.483 --> 00:37:09.784
somebody gets paid.

00:37:10.325 --> 00:37:11.986
Corruption is a culture in Mexico.

00:37:12.046 --> 00:37:15.289
It's endemic to the process of government.

00:37:15.950 --> 00:37:17.631
Mafia exists because of politicians,

00:37:18.051 --> 00:37:20.714
and the government allow them to exist for their own enrichment.

00:37:21.755 --> 00:37:25.598
Quintero would hold parties out at the Rancho Encino Loa,

00:37:26.078 --> 00:37:27.339
and he had a caged lion,

00:37:28.160 --> 00:37:28.841
a couple of them,

00:37:30.022 --> 00:37:31.443
and everybody would be partying,

00:37:31.803 --> 00:37:36.167
and part of the entertainment was he'd throw snitches in the cage and they'd watch him be devoured.

00:37:41.875 --> 00:37:44.317
It was then that Camarena made a major mistake.

00:37:45.217 --> 00:37:46.798
He trusted a Mexican cop.

00:37:50.961 --> 00:37:51.801
They were all there.

00:37:52.622 --> 00:37:54.303
The drug lords and Zorilla.

00:37:55.304 --> 00:37:56.604
Mexico's top cop.

00:37:56.885 --> 00:37:58.766
Like a fat and sassy vulture.

00:37:58.826 --> 00:38:00.347
Enrico Camarena.

00:38:00.887 --> 00:38:03.749
You should not have put your nose in our business.

00:38:03.769 --> 00:38:06.651
Is this the pig who busted my operations in Chihuahua?

00:38:07.451 --> 00:38:09.293
Enrico Camarero Listen to me,

00:38:09.513 --> 00:38:11.054
I work for the DEA

00:38:11.755 --> 00:38:14.717
You just kidnapped a federal agent of the United States government

00:38:15.498 --> 00:38:19.241
Don't worry about us amigo Worry about what we're going to do to you

00:38:20.542 --> 00:38:22.624
Cop, you've got a badge

00:38:23.345 --> 00:38:26.948
Badge? I got no stinking badge

00:38:27.929 --> 00:38:29.170
How the hell can you do this?

00:38:29.930 --> 00:38:32.192
You betrayed us all and your own people for what?

00:38:32.833 --> 00:38:33.433
Money

00:38:34.194 --> 00:38:35.155
Mucho dinero

00:38:37.307 --> 00:38:38.708
Once they had captured Camarena,

00:38:39.029 --> 00:38:41.051
they were determined to find out all he knew.

00:38:52.861 --> 00:38:53.802
I was in bad shape.

00:38:55.484 --> 00:38:57.726
They didn't want me dying before I could tell them everything.

00:38:59.128 --> 00:39:02.170
So they gave me some kind of a drug to make my heart hold out longer.

00:39:06.955 --> 00:39:08.276
They wanted to know everything.

00:39:09.317 --> 00:39:10.138
The names,

00:39:10.659 --> 00:39:11.559
the details,

00:39:12.540 --> 00:39:14.282
how high up the investigation went.

00:39:16.611 --> 00:39:17.412
But I didn't talk.

00:39:18.032 --> 00:39:18.472
If I did,

00:39:18.552 --> 00:39:20.013
other agents would be in my place.

00:39:23.916 --> 00:39:24.256
Actually,

00:39:24.296 --> 00:39:25.797
I wasn't thinking about anyone else.

00:39:26.518 --> 00:39:27.138
I'm no hero.

00:39:27.979 --> 00:39:28.899
I was thinking about me.

00:39:30.020 --> 00:39:30.300
You see,

00:39:30.301 --> 00:39:31.821
when there's no hope and nothing left,

00:39:32.182 --> 00:39:34.123
the only thing you've got is what you have inside.

00:39:36.084 --> 00:39:38.086
I sure as hell wasn't going to give that to them.

00:39:39.146 --> 00:39:40.027
Even if it killed me.

00:39:56.063 --> 00:39:59.844
The cowardly murder of Enrique Kiki Camarena,

00:40:00.624 --> 00:40:02.985
special agent with the Drug Enforcement Administration,

00:40:04.365 --> 00:40:08.567
was carried out by the Mexican government in conjunction,

00:40:09.287 --> 00:40:10.127
in cooperation,

00:40:10.527 --> 00:40:14.968
in partnership with the godfathers of the drug trade.

00:40:18.029 --> 00:40:21.670
The bodies of Camarena and his pilot were found dumped on the roadside.

00:40:22.790 --> 00:40:24.191
Both had been tortured to death.

00:40:26.051 --> 00:40:26.391
U.S.

00:40:26.531 --> 00:40:28.753
law enforcement agents were outraged.

00:40:30.394 --> 00:40:33.055
Enrique Camarena died a soldier in the drug war,

00:40:33.636 --> 00:40:46.323
but his life is not revenged with the prosecution of those people that murdered him or those people that sanctioned that murder or officials of the Mexican government.

00:40:53.855 --> 00:40:57.938
Camarena's murder put the heat on Mexico to clean up the rampant level of corruption.

00:40:58.858 --> 00:41:01.540
But once such a criminally controlled government is established,

00:41:01.980 --> 00:41:04.081
it's nearly impossible to eradicate.

00:41:06.803 --> 00:41:12.907
Law enforcement in the United States were equally frustrated in their efforts to put mob gangsters behind bars.

00:41:14.768 --> 00:41:18.390
Law enforcement changed tactics and began targeting the organizations.

00:41:20.871 --> 00:41:27.035
One of the things we were looking to do was to use the Rico statue to indict the commission,

00:41:27.036 --> 00:41:28.896
the heads of the five New York crime families.

00:41:30.077 --> 00:41:34.720
The Organized Crime Task Force had extraordinary information as to the Lucchese family.

00:41:35.741 --> 00:41:38.964
some evidence as to the heads of one or two others.

00:41:39.384 --> 00:41:43.067
The FBI had bugs in on the heads of three families at the time.

00:41:44.048 --> 00:41:45.509
And so if you combine the two,

00:41:45.869 --> 00:41:52.094
there was a mountain of evidence that could be used to indict and convict all of the family bosses.

00:41:53.395 --> 00:41:54.736
After Jim Brown's death,

00:41:55.116 --> 00:42:00.821
the government successfully used these statues to bring the Jamaican posse's reign of terror to an end.

00:42:01.862 --> 00:42:03.163
The shower posture today

00:42:04.367 --> 00:42:05.468
If it exists at all,

00:42:05.788 --> 00:42:14.034
it exists as a network of people who used to be much more closely aligned in business,

00:42:14.154 --> 00:42:18.757
and their business being narcotics trafficking and weapons trafficking.

00:42:20.238 --> 00:42:21.339
As it exists today,

00:42:21.739 --> 00:42:25.902
they probably are members of,

00:42:26.163 --> 00:42:27.384
if not leaders of,

00:42:27.664 --> 00:42:35.009
smaller groups around the country who simply have a past affiliation with the Shower Posse.

00:42:37.311 --> 00:42:41.174
The people of Taiwan had enough of their government's involvement with the Triads.

00:42:42.687 --> 00:42:43.728
In April 2000,

00:42:43.968 --> 00:42:45.269
President Lee was ousted.

00:42:45.910 --> 00:42:47.811
A spirit of reform swept the country.

00:42:50.153 --> 00:42:51.894
Anti-corruption laws were enacted,

00:42:51.994 --> 00:42:53.655
and many triads were rounded up.

00:42:57.098 --> 00:42:59.260
In response to pressure from the United States,

00:42:59.500 --> 00:43:01.682
a warrant was issued for the arrest of Quintero.

00:43:03.323 --> 00:43:08.046
But the narcotics smuggler bribed his way out of Mexico with a check for a quarter of a million dollars.

00:43:11.455 --> 00:43:14.896
Quintero's immigration papers were signed by the director of police,

00:43:15.536 --> 00:43:16.517
Jose Zoria.

00:43:20.838 --> 00:43:23.859
After the public outcry about Mexico's political corruption,

00:43:24.399 --> 00:43:27.660
Zoria quietly resigned his post and was allowed to leave the country.

00:43:31.841 --> 00:43:34.182
Despite the efforts of a few brave officials,

00:43:34.422 --> 00:43:36.383
Mexico remains troubled by corruption.

00:43:38.423 --> 00:43:41.326
Enrique Camarena was a hero in the fight against drugs,

00:43:42.428 --> 00:43:43.769
but his death meant very little.

00:43:45.872 --> 00:43:47.734
The Mexican drug king still ruled,

00:43:48.135 --> 00:43:50.517
and narcotics still flow across the border.

00:43:53.080 --> 00:43:55.603
As we have seen in our own country and elsewhere,

00:43:56.504 --> 00:43:58.226
organized crime can be beaten.

00:43:58.755 --> 00:44:03.817
The vigilance of law enforcement and courageous politicians who do not bow to money and intimidation,

00:44:04.537 --> 00:44:08.378
the nations of the world can be free from the menace of organized crime.

00:44:09.719 --> 00:44:10.519
I'm Robert Stack.

00:44:11.199 --> 00:44:12.139
Thanks for joining us.

